      "en": {
        "body": [
          "An American Airlines Airbus A321-200, registration N154UW, operating flight AA-1419 from Fort Lauderdale, Florida, to Charlotte, North Carolina, with 230 people on board, was climbing out of Fort Lauderdale's runway 28R when the crew declared PAN PAN, reporting they had hit a flock of birds and had vibrations of the right-hand engine (CFM56).",
          "The crew stopped the climb at 4000 feet and returned to Fort Lauderdale for a safe landing on runway 28R about 20 minutes after departure."
        ],
        "summary": "An American Airlines A321 struck a flock of birds shortly after departing Fort Lauderdale, with vibrations in the right engine; the crew declared PAN PAN and returned for a safe landing about 20 minutes after departure.",
        "title": "American A321 returns to Fort Lauderdale after bird strike on climb-out"
      },
